## The one thing this teaches
**A count array is a bag.** When a question is about *availability* — enough of each item, in any order — a multiset is the model, and for 26 letters the multiset is an `int[26]`.

## Approach
```java
int[] have = new int[26];
for (char c : magazine.toCharArray()) have[c - 'a']++;
for (char c : note.toCharArray()) if (--have[c - 'a'] < 0) return "NO";
return "YES";
```

## Why not `indexOf` and delete
Finding each note letter in the magazine and removing it is O(|note| · |magazine|) and allocates a new string per deletion. The counts discard exactly the information — positions — that the question never needed.

