## The one thing this teaches
**The newcomer fights the top of the stack.** Survivors so far are settled among themselves; a new asteroid can only collide with the most recent right-mover, and if it wins, with the one beneath it — which is exactly a pop loop.

## Approach
```java
Deque<Integer> st = new ArrayDeque<>();   // use the last end as top
for (int x : a) {
    boolean alive = true;
    while (alive && x < 0 && !st.isEmpty() && st.peekLast() > 0) {
        if (st.peekLast() < -x) { st.pollLast(); continue; }   // top explodes, keep fighting
        if (st.peekLast() == -x) st.pollLast();                // both explode
        alive = false;                                         // newcomer is gone
    }
    if (alive) st.addLast(x);
}
```

## The cases that decide it
- `-2 -1 1 2`: nothing collides — left-movers on the left are moving *away*.
- `1 -2 -2 -2`: the first `-2` destroys the `1` and survives; the next `-2`s find a left-mover on top and simply join the stack.

