## The one thing this teaches
**Greedy means keeping the most flexible resource.** The only real decision is how to change a $20. Both options are correct *now*; the difference is what they leave. A $5 can make change for a $10 or a $20, a $10 only helps with a $20, so spend the $10.

## Approach
```java
int fives = 0, tens = 0;
for (int b : bills) {
    if (b == 5) fives++;
    else if (b == 10) { if (fives == 0) return "NO"; fives--; tens++; }
    else if (tens > 0 && fives > 0) { tens--; fives--; }
    else if (fives >= 3) fives -= 3;
    else return "NO";
}
return "YES";
```

