## The one thing this teaches
**Close a part at the first moment it is allowed.** A part starting at `start` must reach the last occurrence of every letter inside it. Growing `end` to cover each letter as it is met, and cutting as soon as `i == end`, gives the shortest valid first part — and a shortest first part leaves the most room for more parts.

## Approach
```java
