for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) last[s.charAt(i) - 'a'] = i;
int start = 0, end = 0;
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    end = Math.max(end, last[s.charAt(i) - 'a']);
    if (i == end) { sizes.add(end - start + 1); start = i + 1; }
}
```

## It is merging intervals
Each letter spans `[first, last]`. Parts are the merged groups of overlapping spans — the sweep above is Merge Intervals with the intervals already in order of start.

