## The one thing this teaches
**An obstacle is a zero in the recurrence.** The unobstructed counting DP needs no special logic for blocked cells: set their count to 0 and the addition does the rest, including blocking everything that could only be reached through them.

## Approach
```java
long[] ways = new long[c];
ways[0] = g[0][0] == '0' ? 1 : 0;
for (int i = 0; i < r; i++)
    for (int j = 0; j < c; j++) {
        if (g[i][j] == '1') ways[j] = 0;
        else if (j > 0) ways[j] = (ways[j] + ways[j - 1]) % MOD;   // above + left
    }
return ways[c - 1];
```

