## The one thing this teaches
**Counting optimal solutions rides along the optimisation DP.** Wherever the DP compares candidates, a count can follow: a strictly better candidate *replaces* the count, an equally good one *adds* to it.

## Approach
```java
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    len[i] = 1; cnt[i] = 1;
    for (int j = 0; j < i; j++) {
        if (a[j] >= a[i]) continue;
        if (len[j] + 1 > len[i]) { len[i] = len[j] + 1; cnt[i] = cnt[j]; }
        else if (len[j] + 1 == len[i]) cnt[i] += cnt[j];
    }
}
// answer: sum of cnt[i] over i with len[i] == max len
```

