## The one thing this teaches
**Exactly = at most − at most one less.** Windows with "at most k" of something shrink and grow monotonically, so the count-all-windows template applies. "Exactly k" does not, but it is the difference of two quantities that do.

## Approach
```java
long atMost(int[] a, int m) {
    if (m < 0) return 0;
    long count = 0;
    int left = 0, odds = 0;
    for (int r = 0; r < a.length; r++) {
        odds += a[r] & 1;
        while (odds > m) odds -= a[left++] & 1;
        count += r - left + 1;
    }
    return count;
}
answer = atMost(a, k) - atMost(a, k - 1);
```

