## Approach
```java
boolean[] seen = new boolean[n];
Deque<Integer> st = new ArrayDeque<>();
st.push(0); seen[0] = true; int visited = 1;
while (!st.isEmpty()) {
    int u = st.pop();
    for (int v : keys.get(u)) if (!seen[v]) { seen[v] = true; visited++; st.push(v); }
}
return visited == n ? "YES" : "NO";
```

## Directed, not undirected
A key to room 3 in room 1 does not mean room 3 opens room 1. Adding edges both ways answers a different, easier question.

