## The one thing this teaches
**Intervals as +1/−1 events.** A half-open interval `[birth, death)` adds 1 at `birth` and removes it at `death`. A prefix sum over those events gives the count at every point — the difference array from Range Addition, with every update adding 1.

## Approach
```java
int[] delta = new int[102];
for (int[] p : people) { delta[p[0] - 1950]++; delta[p[1] - 1950]--; }
int run = 0, best = 0, year = 1950;
for (int i = 0; i < 101; i++) {
    run += delta[i];
    if (run > best) { best = run; year = 1950 + i; }
}
```

## Half-open
A person who dies in 1970 is not counted in 1970, so the −1 lands *at* the death year. And `>` rather than `>=` keeps the earliest year on ties.

