## The one thing this teaches
**A recursive definition answers point queries without being built.** Sₙ has a million characters at n = 20, but each character's value is determined by one position in Sₙ₋₁. Following that one position down the levels is O(n).

## Approach
```java
int bit(int n, long k) {
    if (n == 1) return 0;
    long mid = 1L << (n - 1);
    if (k == mid) return 1;
    if (k < mid) return bit(n - 1, k);
    return 1 - bit(n - 1, (1L << n) - k);      // mirrored and inverted
}
```

## The mirror index
Sₙ has length L = 2ⁿ − 1. Position k on the right corresponds, after reversal, to position L + 1 − k = 2ⁿ − k of Sₙ₋₁. Getting that off by one is the only real risk — check it on S₃ by hand.

