## The one thing this teaches
**Allowed swaps generate every permutation of a connected group.** Adjacent transpositions generate all permutations; so do the transpositions along any connected graph. The question "what can I reach with these swaps?" becomes "which indices are connected?" — a union-find question.

## Approach
```java
for (int[] p : pairs) union(p[0], p[1]);
Map<Integer, List<Integer>> groups = indices grouped by find(i);   // indices ascend naturally
