for (List<Integer> idx : groups.values()) {
    char[] cs = characters of s at idx, sorted;
    for (int j = 0; j < idx.size(); j++) out[idx.get(j)] = cs[j];
}
```

## Why sorted into sorted
To make the string smallest, the earliest position of each group should get its smallest character, the next position the next smallest, and so on — and groups do not interact, so each is optimised independently.

