## The one thing this teaches
**Prefix sums only need to remember what the question asks about.** Subarray Sum Equals K keeps a map of exact sums. Here only parity matters, so the map collapses to two counters.

## Approach
```java
long even = 1, odd = 0, count = 0;   // the empty prefix is even
int parity = 0;
for (int x : a) {
    parity ^= x & 1;                   // & 1 is safe for negatives; % 2 is not
    if (parity == 1) { count += even; odd++; }
    else             { count += odd;  even++; }
}
```

## Negative numbers
In Java, `-3 % 2` is `-1`, not `1`. `x & 1` reads the lowest bit, which is 1 for every odd number in two's complement, negative or not.

