## The one thing this teaches
**Simulate the process on positions, then fill in the values.** The procedure moves cards around without looking at them, so running it on placeholder indices reveals where each value must go.

## Approach
```java
Arrays.sort(cards);
Deque<Integer> q = new ArrayDeque<>();
for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) q.add(i);
int[] deck = new int[n];
for (int card : cards) {
    deck[q.poll()] = card;             // this position is revealed next
    if (!q.isEmpty()) q.add(q.poll()); // the following one goes to the bottom
}
```

## The reverse construction
Alternatively build the deck backwards from the largest card: before placing each card on top, move the bottom card to the top — the reveal steps undone in reverse order.

