## The one thing this teaches
**Find how far a carry can travel.** Adding two arbitrary numbers can carry through a long run of 9s. Doubling cannot: `2 · 9 + 1 = 19` still carries only 1, and whether a carry arrives depends on the next digit alone — so no reversal is needed.

## Approach
```java
if (head.val >= 5) head = new ListNode(0, head);   // room for the new leading 1
for (ListNode p = head; p != null; p = p.next) {
    int carry = (p.next != null && p.next.val >= 5) ? 1 : 0;
    p.val = (p.val * 2) % 10 + carry;
}
return head;
```

## Why the carry never overflows the digit
`(2d) % 10` is even — at most 8 — so adding a carry of 1 gives at most 9.

## Walkthrough: 9 9 9
Prepend 0 (first digit ≥ 5): `0 9 9 9`. Then 0 → 0 + 1, 9 → 8 + 1, 9 → 8 + 1, 9 → 8 + 0: `1 9 9 8`.

