## The one thing this teaches
**A loop inside a loop is fine when the inner one is tiny.** The digit count of a number up to 10^5 takes at most six steps, so the whole scan is effectively linear.

## Approach
```java
int count = 0;
for (int x : a) {
    int digits = 0;
    for (int v = x; v > 0; v /= 10) digits++;
    if (digits % 2 == 0) count++;
}
```

## Three ways to count digits
- repeated division, as above;
- `String.valueOf(x).length()`;
- `(int) Math.log10(x) + 1` — fine for positive values, but floating-point logarithms can be off by one at exact powers of ten on some platforms, so integer methods are safer.

