## The one thing this teaches
**Key the DP by value when the transition names a value.** Longest Increasing Subsequence must consider every smaller earlier element. Here the predecessor is fully determined — `x − difference` — so one map lookup replaces the inner loop.

## Approach
```java
Map<Integer, Integer> best = new HashMap<>();
int answer = 0;
for (int x : a) {
    int len = best.getOrDefault(x - difference, 0) + 1;
    best.put(x, len);          // later copies of x overwrite with a length at least as long
    answer = Math.max(answer, len);
}
```

## Why overwriting is safe
A later occurrence of `x` sees every earlier element, so its length is never shorter than an earlier occurrence's.

## Difference 0
Then `x − difference = x` and the map counts occurrences of each value — the longest subsequence of equal elements.

