## The one thing this teaches
**Unmatched brackets come in two independent kinds.** A `)` that arrives with nothing open, and a `(` still open at the end. Neither can fix the other — a later `(` cannot close an earlier `)` — so the answer is their sum.

## Approach
```java
int open = 0, inserts = 0;
for (char ch : s.toCharArray()) {
    if (ch == '(') open++;
    else if (open > 0) open--;
    else inserts++;          // unmatched ')'
}
return inserts + open;                        // plus unmatched '('
```

## Why greedy matching is optimal
Matching a `)` with the most recent open `(` never hurts: any valid completion can be rearranged to use that pairing.

