## The one thing this teaches
**Reverse a list to get the direction you need.** The survival rule looks right, but a singly linked list only moves left to right. Reversing is O(n) and O(1) space — cheaper than copying into an array.

## Approach
```java
head = reverse(head);
ListNode keep = head;             // the last node always survives
for (ListNode p = head; p.next != null; ) {
    if (p.next.val < keep.val) p.next = p.next.next;    // smaller than something to its right
    else { p = p.next; keep = p; }
}
return reverse(head);
```

## The stack alternative
Walk forward pushing nodes; before pushing, pop every node with a smaller value — it has just found a greater node to its right. The stack, bottom to top, is the answer.

## Strictly greater
Equal values survive: in `1 1 1 1` nothing has a *greater* value to its right.

