21 = 2·9 + 1·3 + 0·1, so base 3 is `210`. The 2 means 9 would be needed twice — NO. For 91 = 81 + 9 + 1, base 3 is `10101` — YES.

## The greedy view
Subtracting the largest power of three not exceeding n, repeatedly, succeeds exactly when each power is used at most once — the same condition, discovered from the top digit down.

