## The one thing this teaches
**Backtracking collapses when choices are forced.** The search looks exponential, but after the first cut the value of every piece is fixed. Only leading zeros leave any freedom in where a piece ends.

## Approach
```java
boolean go(String s, int i, long prev) {
    if (i == s.length()) return true;
    long v = 0;
    for (int j = i; j < s.length(); j++) {
        v = v * 10 + (s.charAt(j) - '0');
        if (v > prev - 1) break;               // only grows from here
        if (v == prev - 1 && go(s, j + 1, v)) return true;
    }
    return false;
}
// try each first piece s[0..k] for k < n − 1
```

## Why break when v exceeds prev − 1
Digits only add to the value as the piece grows, so once it is too large, longer pieces are too large as well.

## Walkthrough: 050043
First piece `05` = 5. Next must be 4: `004` = 4. Next must be 3: `3`. The whole string is used — YES.

